      "side": 1,
      "message": "You may want to use interrupt()/interrupted() to avoid having to use your own boolean and to interrupt accept() automatically. That being said, in principle there is nothing wrong using your own boolean and I think close() will eject the control from accept() so this is fine.\nIn this case however I think you have a problem where there was an exception and at the same time tearDown() is called, where the control reaching here finds `mIsRunning` false but the socket isn\u0027t closed yet and the exception had some other cause. In that case, IIUC you should postDestroy but you won\u0027t.\n\nI think you may not have a way out of a lock for this, because you do need to synchronize multiple instructions.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 318,
        "startChar": 29,
        "endLine": 318,
        "endChar": 39
      },
      "revId": "241cddfb9af2e4fe45276afe682243b9a9fae8dd",
